                    briefing_text_r3:       `Mid-season the rival drops price another 8% and a Ramadan influencer campaign goes viral — and HQ emails asking why Türkiye's consistency score is trending down. You have no new money: the ₺240M is frozen, so a broad price war just burns it. Reallocate fast. Your award last year was for <strong>speed</strong>, so weigh a good-enough plan locked in week three against a perfect plan delivered after the window closes. And re-run your ROI in <em>today's lira</em> — imported inputs are up ~15%, so promotions that paid back last year may not now. Decide what to tell HQ in four lines.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Defend agility & lock the plan`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Pitch the locked H2 plan to the HQ Global Brand Director and the GM at the September council. Show that responsiveness and standardization were managed as <strong>complementary twin engines</strong>, not a zero-sum fight — name the standardized asset that carried local relevance. Commit to a 90-day agility scorecard tracking share, consistency and ROI together, and make the case for the subsidiary's autonomy: <em>you keep the right to run your own market only if consistency stayed above the floor while agility delivered.</em> Defend the complementarity with conviction.`,

