                    insight_leader:         `Agile glocal leader: you ran the twin engines together — defending Bella's share through the Ramadan window while keeping the Brand Consistency Index above HQ's floor and ROI healthy under the lira shock. You proved standardization and local responsiveness are complementary, not a trade-off.`,
                    insight_compliant:      `Compliant but you lost the season: consistency is safe and HQ is delighted, but the rival took the Ramadan window and Bella's share fell below the floor. ‘We followed the 70% rule’ is not a performance story — standardization without market orientation forfeits the local engine.`,
                    insight_rogue:          `You won the quarter but the autonomy is at risk: share held, yet the Brand Consistency Index fell below 80 and HQ has put Türkiye's marketing autonomy under review. Treating standardization as expendable can win the season and lose the right to run your own market.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short on the twin engines — share, consistency and ROI didn't all clear their floors. Re-examine where global and local were forced into a seesaw instead of one asset doing double duty.`,
                    insight_breach:         `The Brand Consistency Index breached the 80 floor — HQ triggers an autonomy review. Localising heavily defends share but, pushed too far, costs the subsidiary the discretion to run its own market.`,
                    insight_shareloss:      `Bella's value share fell below the 18% floor. The rival's value tier owned the Ramadan/wedding window — an estimated 3–4 points of share, hundreds of millions of lira in annualised sales, that went unanswered.`,
                    insight_margin:         `ROI stayed weak: under the ~15% lira-driven cost rise, too much budget went to promotions that barely break even. Margin-aware allocation is the difference between activity and return.`,
                    insight_opaque:         `You deviated from the mandate without telling HQ, and they learned it from the consistency tracker rather than from you. Even a strong result can't buy back the credibility — opaque deviation weakens the case for autonomy.`,
                    insight_complementary:  `This is the complementarity the research is about: a standardized asset adapted for the local occasion let one lira buy both consistency and relevance. The twin engines reinforced each other instead of fighting.`,

                    hint_breach:            `Brand Consistency has breached the 80 floor — HQ autonomy review is in play. Bring global weight back up or lean on assets that carry local relevance without leaving the brand.`,
                    hint_share:             `Bella's share is below the 18% floor — the rival is owning the season. Put more of the local budget into the Ramadan/wedding occasion where the share is bleeding.`,
                    hint_margin:            `ROI is weak under the lira shock. Stop funding broad discounts and re-run every activity at today's input costs — fund only what still pays back.`,
                    hint_opaque:            `You've deviated from the mandate without squaring it with HQ. Get ahead of the consistency tracker with a transparent business case before HQ finds it.`,
                    hint_agility:           `Marketing Agility is lagging — you're reacting slowly or treating the engines as a seesaw. Move faster in-season and find the asset that serves both global and local at once.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — share, consistency and agility all healthy. Lock a full scorecard with named owners so the in-season gains survive past the council.`,

